# Requirements Specification — {{project_name}}

<!-- GEN: Why: the fixed grilling process defines how to interview and gate; this skill defines what to ask, write, and verify in this workspace on one screen. Kind: Mandatory — keep the purpose, adapt the structure (core/authoring-guide.md). -->
<!-- GEN: Description: follow core/authoring-guide.md "Description" — workspace name, concrete situations, the team's own trigger words (their language allowed), an "even if" clause; check it against the trial prompts (Step 8). -->

This skill supplies workspace-specific rules to the Coder Nexus `grilling` process, `gate-review` spec mode, and `requirements.md` template. All fixed gates, laws, and validated template sections remain unchanged.

## 1. Deterministic Verification Gates (`PASS` / `FAIL`)

<!-- GEN: Binary CLI gates run before presenting Gate 1 (exit 0 / 0 invalid matches = PASS; otherwise FAIL). -->
| Gate | Command | Enforces |
|---|---|---|
| Spec & delta validator | `{{validator_command}}` | `requirements.md`, `codebase-notes.md`, and `change-impact.md` structural and ID rules |
| Banned vague-word audit | `{{rg_vague_words_command}}` | Zero unquantified vague words in `requirements.md` (`RS4`) |
| Banned synonym audit | `{{rg_synonyms_command}}` | Verbatim `domain-knowledge` glossary terms; zero `"Avoid saying"` synonyms (`RS5`) |
| Open question & AC traceability check | `{{rg_open_questions_command}}` | Zero `OPEN` `Q-NN` in `codebase-notes.md` and every `AC-NN` traced to `BR-NN` / `G-NN` (`RS4`, `RS6`) |

## 2. Mandatory Specification Principles (`RS1`–`RS10`)

<!-- GEN: Every rule RS1–RS10 is mandatory compliance. No per-rule severity column; Gate 1 findings use BLOCKER / MAJOR / MINOR. -->
| Rule | Mandatory Principle | Why | Reference |
|---|---|---|---|
| `RS1` | Read all mapped sources first; resolve conflicts by source priority; never guess unreachable sources | Keeps the Source Inventory accurate from turn 1 | [01]({{ref_01}}) |
| `RS2` | Ask one question at a time per `grilling` dimension, recommendation first, citing its `G-NN` | Shortens grilling and prevents scope drift | [01]({{ref_01}}) |
| `RS3` | Check every mandatory domain edge-case category or record `not applicable` with a reason | Catches recurring domain defects before design | [02]({{ref_02}}) |
| `RS4` | Write observable `BR-NN` / `AC-NN` and measurable `G-NN` signals; replace banned vague words or raise `Q-NN` | Ensures QA testability and unambiguous user approval | [02]({{ref_02}}) |
| `RS5` | Use `domain-knowledge` glossary terms verbatim across goals, `BR-NN`, `AC-NN`, and scenarios | Prevents synonym drift across spec and code | [02]({{ref_02}}) |
| `RS6` | Run `PASS` / `FAIL` CLI checks and Gate 1 review questions (`[Gap]` / `[Ambiguity]` / `[Conflict]`) before approval | Presents Gate 1 only when 0 `OPEN` `Q-NN` remain | [03]({{ref_03}}) |
| `RS7` | Include environment (`DEV` / `STG` / `PROD`), reproduction steps, expected vs actual, impact, and regression scope on bugs | Gives root-cause debugging and QA exact diagnostic facts | [02]({{ref_02}}) |
| `RS8` | Write user-facing documents in {{team_language}}; keep code symbols and identifiers in English | Lets stakeholders review in their language while matching code | [01]({{ref_01}}) |
| `RS9` | Keep all fixed `grilling` laws, `gate-review` steps, and `requirements.md` sections intact | Preserves handshake compatibility across agents | [01]({{ref_01}}) |
| `RS10` | Classify `v2+` changes as `ADDED` / `MODIFIED` / `REMOVED` against baseline code with `REMOVED` migration notes | Makes behavioral deltas and data migrations explicit | [02]({{ref_02}}) |

Gate 1 review findings are tagged `[Gap]` / `[Ambiguity]` / `[Conflict]` and graded strictly on the unified `BLOCKER` / `MAJOR` / `MINOR` scale (`shared_contracts/flags_and_statuses.md`).

